<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">4 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 4 September, from 476 to 1998.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/odoacer" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/odoacer.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">476 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,550 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Odoacer deposes Romulus Augustulus, the last Western emperor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Germanic commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odoacer">Odoacer</a> deposed the boy emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romulus-augustulus">Romulus Augustulus</a> and sent the imperial regalia to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>. The date is conventionally taken as the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-roman-empire">Western Roman Empire</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-roman-empire">Western Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romulus-augustulus">Romulus Augustulus</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odoacer">Odoacer</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1781 CE <span class="tih-ago">245 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Spanish settlers found the pueblo of Los Angeles</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Forty-four settlers of mixed Spanish, Native and African ancestry founded a farming town near the Porciúncula River. El Pueblo de la Reina de los Ángeles grew into the second-largest US city.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1888 CE <span class="tih-ago">138 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">George Eastman patents the Kodak roll-film camera</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">George Eastman received a patent for his Kodak box camera. Sold pre-loaded with film under the slogan 'You press the button, we do the rest', it made photography a mass pastime.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1957 CE <span class="tih-ago">69 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Arkansas National Guard blocks Black students at Little Rock</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Governor Orval Faubus used the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-guard-panama">National Guard</a> to stop nine Black students entering Little Rock Central High School. Later in the month <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dwight-d-eisenhower">Eisenhower</a> sent federal troops to enforce desegregation.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1998 CE <span class="tih-ago">28 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Larry Page and Sergey Brin incorporate Google</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Two Stanford PhD students incorporated Google, working from a rented garage in Menlo Park. Its search engine became the gateway to the web and the company one of the world's most valuable.</p></div></li></ol>
